{"id": "gsm8k:591", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790750388.174938, "first_event_seconds": 0.9322241990012117, "wall_seconds": 10.905270913965069, "prompt_sha256": "b325453bba958b796ceffa32c94af4dc85815ce182e913ceac5ce28581b7416f", "prompt_tokens": 169, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 214, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "2da78dea34d4470f977bd4a463881964", "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. The first dog is an Affenpinscher, who weighs 10 pounds.\n2. The next dog is a Dachshund, who weighs twice as much as the Affenpinscher. Therefore, the Dachshund weighs:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 10 = 20 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n3. The next dog is a Papillon, who weighs one-fourth as much as the Dachshund. Therefore, the Papillon weighs:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{20}{4} = 5 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n4. The last dog is a Mastiff, who weighs 44 times the weight of the Papillon. Therefore, the Mastiff weighs:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 5 = 220 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the weight of the Mastiff is \\(\\boxed{220}\\) pounds.", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "220", "gsm_numeric_answer": "220", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 214, "entry_transfer_id": "9a83d8d2-c6f9-46d8-bcc7-2fe09a475f43", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.00339623901527375, "arm": "full", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
