{"id": "gsm8k:405", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790750489.8517432, "first_event_seconds": 0.9135631839744747, "wall_seconds": 21.42690139997285, "prompt_sha256": "85badf675cba1a7e81abbd81ded5ce45cc8babf3f28f71b4dd22197c86fdca5d", "prompt_tokens": 143, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 418, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "2c38dc126fdc48cebfaa2d5e97af34f0", "text": "To determine how much money Tyson would spend on the meat and cheese, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of sandwiches needed:**\n   Each sandwich serves 4 people. There are 20 people in total.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of sandwiches} = \\frac{20 \\text{ people}}{4 \\text{ people per sandwich}} = 5 \\text{ sandwiches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the amount of meat and cheese needed:**\n   Each sandwich requires 1 pound of meat and 1 pound of cheese.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total pounds of meat} = 5 \\text{ sandwiches} \\times 1 \\text{ pound per sandwich} = 5 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total pounds of cheese} = 5 \\text{ sandwiches} \\times 1 \\text{ pound per sandwich} = 5 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost of the meat:**\n   The cost of meat is $7.00 per pound.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of meat} = 5 \\text{ pounds} \\times 7 \\text{ dollars per pound} = 35 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the cost of the cheese:**\n   The cost of cheese is $3.00 per pound.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of cheese} = 5 \\text{ pounds} \\times 3 \\text{ dollars per pound} = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = \\text{Cost of meat} + \\text{Cost of cheese} = 35 \\text{ dollars} + 15 \\text{ dollars} = 50 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nFinal answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{50}\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "50", "gsm_numeric_answer": "50", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 418, "entry_transfer_id": "e9821be7-8046-43a3-8f36-65fe15