{"id": "gsm8k:449", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790751572.2630727, "first_event_seconds": 0.8774244890082628, "wall_seconds": 11.170667294994928, "prompt_sha256": "4a2639fdf7649797d63dcff52f916cc191047f04bcdcefa56a4c10ac60ba145a", "prompt_tokens": 98, "max_new_tokens": 512, "completion_tokens": 228, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "910ea440d4e5420db51f3856fbdfac9f", "text": "To determine the total number of crayons Beatrice bought, we need to calculate the number of crayons in each type of packet and then sum them up.\n\n1. Calculate the number of crayons in the six packets that each contain 8 pieces:\n   \\[\n   6 \\text{ packets} \\times 8 \\text{ crayons per packet} = 48 \\text{ crayons}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of crayons in the four packets that each contain 16 pieces:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ packets} \\times 16 \\text{ crayons per packet} = 64 \\text{ crayons}\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the number of crayons from both types of packets to find the total number of crayons:\n   \\[\n   48 \\text{ crayons} + 64 \\text{ crayons} = 112 \\text{ crayons}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of crayons Beatrice bought is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{112}\n\\]", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "112", "gsm_numeric_answer": "112", "gsm_extraction": "last_number", "truncated": false, "events": 228, "entry_transfer_id": "d2976db7-36d5-46b9-aeed-e7f620614e54", "completed_entry_released": true, "cleanup_seconds": 0.003906829981133342, "arm": "full", "dataset_sha256": "5591e964da8fd457f0e113d82330c84c94e6074b1ad80d1ee414dca751d893c3"}
